From: liviyifan <344781483+liviyifan@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] [AArch64] ILP32: use the small code model for JIT by default

The JIT default on AArch64 is the large code model, which ILP32 does not
have: there are no relocations for 64-bit absolute addresses, and the
object writer stops with "absolute MOV relocation is not supported in
ILP32". All ILP32 addresses are below 4 GiB, within the reach of ADRP, so
the small code model always works. A code model that is asked for
explicitly is not changed.

Signed-off-by: liviyifan <344781483+liviyifan@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 llvm/lib/Target/AArch64/AArch64TargetMachine.cpp | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/llvm/lib/Target/AArch64/AArch64TargetMachine.cpp b/llvm/lib/Target/AArch64/AArch64TargetMachine.cpp
index bc51ab1f5..c8b1d844e 100644
--- a/llvm/lib/Target/AArch64/AArch64TargetMachine.cpp
+++ b/llvm/lib/Target/AArch64/AArch64TargetMachine.cpp
@@ -348,7 +348,10 @@ getEffectiveAArch64CodeModel(const Triple &TT,
   // We should set the CodeModel::Small for Windows ARM64 in JIT mode,
   // since with large code model LLVM generating 4 MOV instructions, and
   // Windows doesn't support relocating these long branch (4 MOVs).
-  if (JIT && !TT.isOSWindows())
+  // The ILP32 ABI has no large code model (it lacks the relocations for
+  // 64-bit absolute addresses), and with 32-bit addresses everything is
+  // within the reach of ADRP.
+  if (JIT && !TT.isOSWindows() && !TT.isILP32Environment())
     return CodeModel::Large;
   return CodeModel::Small;
 }
